ools across the  country don't have a full-time nurse and  25% don't have a nurse at all is that  acceptable it's not acceptable students  deserve what they need in order to be in  school and ready to learn ma Zeke blames  shrinking budgets for the shortfall  which she says increases the burden on  existing nurses and puts kids at risk if  you have a workload that doesn't enable  you to care for the students in the way  they need it's like drinking water from  a fire hose so now time for school  number two yes my elementary school dean  Igor B crease is a school nurse in  Howard County Maryland who covers two  schools a day I'm often stressed because  I have to figure out the safest way to  balance it she has health assistants at  each school who call her with questions  when she's not in the building  if I'm busy with an emergency at my  other school I'm not available right  away so it might delay there at their  care song as a school nurse do you feel  like you're stretched too thin I think  so I would love to be able to be in one  place so that I could provide the care  that the kids need I  my nose in Cincinnati Ohio where nurses  were also sometimes covering more than  one school they're tackling the problem  through a partnership with Cincinnati  Children's Hospital we now are able to  provide routine primary care services  for all of the students in the building  as well as any child in the community  they've opened house centers in schools  to close the gap so students get  services here no different than they do  in a pediatricians office in the wake of  his son's death Roisin Presley says  schools must find a way to provide care  for all students they're being I know  nurses at the school you might as well  miles along teachers teaching kids at  home that's just common sense the  Philadelphia School District is working  with a local hospital to determine if  and what kind of additional health  support is needed in the schools and  next month a bill will be reintroduced  in Washington called the nurse Act it  would provide grants for schools to hire  nurses good our priorities need to  change this is an issue heart goes out  to the fuzzies listen they said listen  we don't know if the nurse would have  made a difference but at least you would  have known everything would have been  done to help them try thank you that's  what they say a school nurse just should  have been that exactly we should say for  our school matter series CBS this  morning partnered with USA Today to  feature extended stories and  investigations on education so go to  usatoday.com for a new article published  this morning on the increasing demands  for school nurses as students mental and  physical health problems increase we  will be right back
 

